WEBVTT

00:02.522 --> 00:03.647
Water.

00:04.941 --> 00:06.316
Earth.

00:06.859 --> 00:08.402
Fire.

00:09.028 --> 00:10.320
Air.

00:11.239 --> 00:14.616
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.451 --> 00:19.246
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.706 --> 00:22.582
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.667 --> 00:23.750
could stop them.

00:23.835 --> 00:26.628
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

00:27.422 --> 00:28.463
100 years passed,

00:28.548 --> 00:31.258
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

00:31.342 --> 00:32.843
an airbender named Aang.

00:33.136 --> 00:35.220
And although
his airbending skills are great,

00:35.305 --> 00:38.473
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone,

00:39.100 --> 00:42.102
But I believe Aang can save the world.

00:56.367 --> 00:57.367
Look!

01:04.292 --> 01:05.667
He is taunting us.

01:06.753 --> 01:08.211
You are so going to be dinner.

01:10.631 --> 01:12.716
Hey, where's the fishing line?

01:12.800 --> 01:15.302
I didn't think
you would need it, Sokka.

01:16.304 --> 01:17.846
It's all tangled.

01:18.681 --> 01:20.432
Not tangled, woven.

01:20.516 --> 01:22.184
I made you a necklace, Katara.

01:22.769 --> 01:24.895
I thought since you lost
your other one...

01:28.191 --> 01:29.191
Thanks, Aang.

01:29.275 --> 01:30.275
I love it.

01:30.610 --> 01:31.693
Great, Aang.

01:31.778 --> 01:33.278
Maybe instead of saving the world,

01:33.363 --> 01:34.988
you can go
into the jewelry-making business.

01:35.531 --> 01:37.115
I don't see why I can't do both.

01:40.787 --> 01:42.079
Stop taunting me!

01:45.958 --> 01:47.376
So, how do I look?

01:53.091 --> 01:55.300
You mean, all of you
or just your neck--

01:55.385 --> 01:57.219
I mean, because they both look great.

01:57.595 --> 01:58.929
Smoochie smoochie.

01:59.222 --> 02:01.473
Someone's in love.

02:02.141 --> 02:03.767
I, well--

02:04.268 --> 02:05.644
Stop teasing him, Sokka.

02:05.978 --> 02:07.479
Aang's just a good friend,

02:07.563 --> 02:10.357
a sweet little guy, just like Momo.

02:10.650 --> 02:11.650
Thanks.

02:17.448 --> 02:19.408
Someone's being attacked
by a platypus bear!

02:32.046 --> 02:33.088
Well, hello there.

02:33.840 --> 02:35.382
Nice day, isn't it?

02:35.550 --> 02:37.008
Make noise! He'll run off!

02:37.093 --> 02:38.969
No, play dead! He'll lose interest!

02:39.554 --> 02:42.347
Whoa, close one. Ha ha ha.

02:43.099 --> 02:44.766
Run downhill, then climb a tree!

02:44.851 --> 02:46.351
No, punch him in the bill!

02:46.436 --> 02:47.894
And then run in zig-zags.

02:48.646 --> 02:49.729
No need.

02:49.814 --> 02:51.106
It's going to be fine.

02:58.531 --> 02:59.531
Whoa, there.

03:09.542 --> 03:11.209
Lunch.

03:12.503 --> 03:14.296
Lucky for you we came along.

03:14.505 --> 03:17.966
Thanks, but everything
was already under control.

03:18.426 --> 03:19.801
Not to worry.

03:19.886 --> 03:22.804
Aunt Wu predicted
I'd have a safe journey.

03:23.181 --> 03:24.181
Aunt who?

03:24.265 --> 03:25.849
No, Aunt Wu.

03:25.933 --> 03:28.560
She's the fortune-teller
from my village.

03:29.353 --> 03:31.313
Awful nice knowing your future.

03:31.397 --> 03:33.315
Wow, it must be.

03:33.608 --> 03:35.358
That explains why you were so calm.

03:35.776 --> 03:37.736
But the fortune-teller was wrong.

03:37.862 --> 03:39.070
You didn't have a safe journey.

03:39.155 --> 03:40.197
You were almost killed.

03:40.865 --> 03:42.032
But I wasn't.

03:42.116 --> 03:43.909
All right, have a good one.

03:46.496 --> 03:50.415
And Aunt Wu said if I met
any travelers, to give them this.

03:54.670 --> 03:57.047
Maybe we should go see Aunt Wu
and learn our fortunes.

03:57.131 --> 03:58.423
It could be fun.

03:58.508 --> 04:01.384
Come on.
Fortune-telling is nonsense.

04:02.470 --> 04:03.470
What do you know?

04:03.554 --> 04:04.554
An umbrella.

04:06.974 --> 04:07.974
That proves it.

04:08.059 --> 04:09.226
No, it doesn't.

04:09.644 --> 04:11.728
You can't really tell the future.

04:11.812 --> 04:14.231
I guess you're not
really getting wet, then.

04:14.774 --> 04:17.526
Whoa-- Aah!

04:17.944 --> 04:18.944
Of course she predicted

04:19.028 --> 04:20.028
it was gonna rain.

04:20.112 --> 04:21.446
The sky has been grey all day.

04:21.531 --> 04:23.281
Just admit you might be wrong,

04:23.366 --> 04:24.741
and you can come under the umbrella.

04:25.785 --> 04:27.577
Look, I'm gonna
predict the future now.

04:27.662 --> 04:30.497
It's going to keep drizzling.

04:31.958 --> 04:33.250
See?

04:34.961 --> 04:36.753
Not everyone has the gift, Sokka.

04:40.383 --> 04:41.383
Aah!

04:56.524 --> 04:59.276
Aunt Wu is expecting you.

04:59.652 --> 05:00.944
Really?

05:01.028 --> 05:02.112
Pfft.

05:06.492 --> 05:10.078
My name is Meng,
and I'm Aunt Wu's assistant.

05:15.334 --> 05:16.793
Well, hello there.

05:18.212 --> 05:19.254
Hello.

05:19.338 --> 05:20.672
Can I get you some tea

05:20.756 --> 05:23.174
or some of Aunt Wu's
special bean curd puffs?

05:23.634 --> 05:24.634
I'll try a curd puff.

05:24.719 --> 05:25.719
Just a second.

05:26.137 --> 05:27.137
So, what's your name?

05:27.221 --> 05:28.221
Aang.

05:28.806 --> 05:30.599
That rhymes with Meng,

05:30.683 --> 05:33.476
and you've got some pretty big ears,
don't you?

05:34.478 --> 05:35.937
I guess.

05:36.355 --> 05:37.564
Don't be modest.

05:37.648 --> 05:38.648
They're huge.

05:38.983 --> 05:41.443
Well, Aang, it's very nice
to meet you--

05:41.902 --> 05:43.069
Very nice.

05:43.154 --> 05:44.446
Likewise.

05:45.364 --> 05:46.656
I can't believe we're here

05:46.741 --> 05:47.949
in the house of nonsense.

05:48.367 --> 05:50.577
Try to keep an open mind, Sokka.

05:50.661 --> 05:51.828
There are things in this world

05:51.912 --> 05:53.330
that just can't be explained.

05:53.414 --> 05:55.999
Wouldn't it be nice to have
some insight into your future?

05:56.083 --> 05:58.501
It would be nice
to have some bean curd puffs.

06:00.546 --> 06:02.047
Meng!

06:02.131 --> 06:04.924
Aunt Wu says
I'm going to meet my true love!

06:05.343 --> 06:08.178
He's going to give me
a rare panda lily.

06:08.471 --> 06:10.889
That's so romantic.

06:11.474 --> 06:14.976
I wonder if my true love
will give me a rare flower.

06:15.061 --> 06:16.353
Good luck with that.

06:17.605 --> 06:20.899
Is that the big-eared guy
who Aunt Wu predicted you'd marry?

06:24.862 --> 06:25.862
Aah!

06:29.575 --> 06:30.825
Enjoy your snack.

06:33.204 --> 06:35.455
Welcome, young travelers.

06:35.539 --> 06:36.665
Now, who's next?

06:37.291 --> 06:38.917
Don't be shy.

06:42.213 --> 06:43.672
I guess that's me.

06:44.924 --> 06:46.883
Not bad, not bad.

06:50.680 --> 06:52.138
I'm good on puffs.

06:54.225 --> 06:57.727
So, what do you think
they're talking about back there?

06:57.812 --> 06:59.270
Boring stuff, I'm sure.

06:59.355 --> 07:00.939
Love, who she's gonna marry,

07:01.023 --> 07:02.732
how many babies she's gonna have.

07:02.817 --> 07:05.235
Yeah, dumb stuff like that.

07:05.861 --> 07:07.404
Well, I gotta find a bathroom.

07:12.576 --> 07:14.494
Your palms are so smooth.

07:14.578 --> 07:16.913
Do you use moisturizer?

07:16.997 --> 07:19.791
Actually,
I have this special seaweed lotion.

07:20.042 --> 07:22.210
I could get you some if you want.

07:22.294 --> 07:25.547
So, do you see anything
interesting in my love line?

07:25.631 --> 07:28.216
I see a great romance for you--

07:28.801 --> 07:30.301
The man you're going to marry.

07:30.386 --> 07:31.720
Tell me more!

07:31.804 --> 07:35.849
I can see
that he's a very powerful bender.

07:43.733 --> 07:46.025
Looks like someone
had a pretty good bathroom break.

07:46.861 --> 07:48.486
Yeah, when I was in there--

07:48.571 --> 07:49.738
I don't even want to know.

07:49.822 --> 07:50.989
Who's next?

07:51.073 --> 07:53.116
Ok, let's get this over with.

07:53.451 --> 07:56.703
Your future is full
of struggle and anguish,

07:56.787 --> 07:59.664
most of it self-inflicted.

08:00.124 --> 08:02.041
But you didn't read
my palms or anything.

08:02.460 --> 08:03.752
I don't need to.

08:03.836 --> 08:05.545
It's written all over your face.

08:08.549 --> 08:11.050
You there, come with me.

08:13.137 --> 08:16.473
This is the most reliable method
of telling your fortune.

08:16.932 --> 08:18.516
The bones never lie.

08:19.059 --> 08:20.769
Go on. Pick one.

08:22.897 --> 08:24.647
Now throw it on the fire.

08:25.608 --> 08:28.026
The heat makes cracks in the bones,

08:28.444 --> 08:31.696
and I read the bone cracks
to tell your destiny.

08:33.157 --> 08:35.074
Wow, that's a big crack.

08:36.619 --> 08:38.286
I've never seen this before.

08:41.999 --> 08:43.166
My!

08:49.924 --> 08:52.717
Your destiny-- This is incredible.

08:52.802 --> 08:56.513
You will be involved
in a great battle--

08:56.597 --> 09:00.391
An awesome conflict
between the forces of good and evil.

09:00.476 --> 09:05.063
A battle whose outcome will determine
the fate of the whole world.

09:05.314 --> 09:07.148
Yeah, yeah. I knew that already,

09:07.233 --> 09:08.817
But did it say anything about a girl?

09:09.193 --> 09:10.235
A girl?

09:10.319 --> 09:11.986
You want to know about love?

09:12.071 --> 09:13.196
Yes!

09:13.906 --> 09:15.615
I'm sorry, but I didn't see anything.

09:18.369 --> 09:19.577
Look!

09:19.662 --> 09:21.371
I must have missed something.

09:21.872 --> 09:23.122
Right here.

09:23.207 --> 09:28.336
It says, "trust your heart, and you
will be with the one you love."

09:28.671 --> 09:29.838
Really?

09:29.922 --> 09:31.089
Thank you, Aunt Wu!

09:34.093 --> 09:35.718
Well, now you got to see
for yourselves

09:35.803 --> 09:38.221
that fortune-telling
is just a big, stupid hoax.

09:38.472 --> 09:39.681
You're just saying that

09:39.765 --> 09:41.850
because you're gonna make yourself
unhappy your whole life.

09:41.934 --> 09:43.560
That woman is crazy!

09:44.019 --> 09:47.605
My life will be calm and happy
and joyful!

09:50.651 --> 09:52.318
That doesn't prove anything.

09:52.403 --> 09:54.279
Well, I liked my predictions.

09:54.697 --> 09:57.156
Certain things
are gonna turn out very well.

09:57.408 --> 09:58.950
They sure are.

09:59.034 --> 10:00.118
Why?

10:00.202 --> 10:01.202
What did she tell you?

10:01.662 --> 10:02.662
Some stuff.

10:02.746 --> 10:03.746
You'll find out.

10:09.295 --> 10:10.461
What's with the sky?

10:10.921 --> 10:13.506
We're waiting for Aunt Wu
to come and read the clouds

10:13.591 --> 10:15.508
to predict the fate
of the whole village.

10:15.593 --> 10:17.760
That cloud kind of looks
like a fluffy bunny.

10:18.304 --> 10:20.346
You better hope that's not a bunny.

10:20.431 --> 10:23.474
The fluffy bunny cloud
forecasts doom and destruction.

10:23.851 --> 10:25.476
Do you even hear yourself?

10:25.978 --> 10:27.979
The cloud reading
will tell us if Mount Makapu

10:28.063 --> 10:30.148
will remain dormant for another year

10:30.232 --> 10:31.232
or if it will erupt.

10:31.734 --> 10:33.860
We used to have
a tradition once a year

10:33.944 --> 10:35.111
of going up the mountain

10:35.195 --> 10:36.863
to check the volcano ourselves,

10:37.281 --> 10:38.907
But ever since Aunt Wu

10:38.991 --> 10:40.992
moved to the village 20 years ago,

10:41.076 --> 10:44.203
we have a tradition of not doing that.

10:44.538 --> 10:46.539
I can't believe
you would trust your lives

10:46.624 --> 10:48.708
to that crazy
old woman's superstition!

10:49.293 --> 10:50.835
Shh! She's coming.

10:54.924 --> 10:56.341
Hey, Aang,

10:56.425 --> 10:59.594
don't you think that cloud
looks like a flower?

11:00.304 --> 11:02.180
Sure, I guess.

11:02.890 --> 11:05.433
Hey, Katara, don't you think
that cloud looks like a flower?

11:05.517 --> 11:06.559
Shh!

11:13.275 --> 11:15.443
Bending arrow cloud--

11:15.527 --> 11:19.072
Good crops this year.
Nice, big harvest.

11:19.406 --> 11:21.449
Darn good news!

11:21.867 --> 11:25.453
Wavy moon-shaped cloud-- Let's see.

11:26.080 --> 11:28.915
Gonna be a great year for twins.

11:29.249 --> 11:30.333
-Yes!
-Yes!

11:31.001 --> 11:35.171
And a cumulus cloud with a twisty
nub coming off the end of it--

11:35.756 --> 11:40.259
The village will not be destroyed
by the volcano this year!

11:42.346 --> 11:43.972
Since I got you here,

11:44.056 --> 11:46.140
there's something I want to tell you.

11:46.308 --> 11:48.476
I like you, but more than normal.

11:50.854 --> 11:51.854
Never mind.

11:58.737 --> 11:59.862
Hi, Aunt Wu.

11:59.947 --> 12:01.072
Sorry to bother you.

12:01.156 --> 12:02.281
Anytime.

12:02.366 --> 12:04.325
About this man I'm supposed to marry--

12:04.410 --> 12:05.618
Is he gonna be handsome?

12:05.703 --> 12:06.911
I hope he's tall.

12:07.538 --> 12:10.415
You want another reading.

12:10.624 --> 12:11.624
Yes, please.

12:14.712 --> 12:16.546
I can't believe all these saps.

12:16.964 --> 12:19.215
Someone really needs
to scream some sense at them.

12:19.591 --> 12:21.259
They seem happy, Sokka.

12:21.343 --> 12:22.677
Not for long.

12:22.761 --> 12:25.179
I'm gonna prove
Aunt Wu's predictions are nonsense.

12:26.098 --> 12:27.140
Hey, you,

12:27.224 --> 12:29.934
I bet Aunt Wu told you to wear
those red shoes, didn't she?

12:30.019 --> 12:32.311
Yeah, she said
I'd be wearing red shoes

12:32.396 --> 12:33.646
when I met my true love.

12:35.107 --> 12:36.607
And how many times
have you worn those shoes

12:36.692 --> 12:37.942
since you got that fortune?

12:38.027 --> 12:39.277
Every day.

12:40.195 --> 12:42.530
Then of course it's gonna come true!

12:43.073 --> 12:44.741
Really? You think so?

12:44.825 --> 12:46.576
I'm so excited!

12:49.496 --> 12:52.206
Aah! Uhh!

12:53.083 --> 12:55.585
And then you'll have
your third great grandchild

12:55.669 --> 12:58.713
before quietly
passing away in your sleep.

12:58.797 --> 13:00.423
Is that enough information for you?

13:00.883 --> 13:03.509
Wow. Thanks, Aunt Wu.

13:03.594 --> 13:05.428
Wait. One more thing.

13:05.888 --> 13:08.097
How warmly should I dress tomorrow?

13:08.432 --> 13:10.433
You want me to do a reading for that?

13:12.102 --> 13:14.395
I don't care what Aunt Wu told you!

13:14.480 --> 13:16.814
You have to take a bath sometime!

13:20.903 --> 13:23.863
So, Sokka, you know some stuff
about ladies, right?

13:23.947 --> 13:25.114
Some stuff?

13:25.199 --> 13:26.908
You've come to the right place.

13:26.992 --> 13:28.409
What can I do you for?

13:28.827 --> 13:30.286
Well, there's this girl...

13:32.456 --> 13:34.332
I think I know who you mean.

13:34.666 --> 13:36.501
You do? And you're ok with it?

13:36.585 --> 13:37.919
Of course I am.

13:38.003 --> 13:39.295
And to tell you the truth,

13:39.379 --> 13:41.339
I've been picking up
a subtle vibe that she likes you, too.

13:41.507 --> 13:42.507
She does?

13:42.800 --> 13:44.801
Yeah. She's crazy about you.

13:44.885 --> 13:47.053
All you have to do now
is not mess it up.

13:47.471 --> 13:48.971
Well, how do I do that?

13:49.056 --> 13:51.224
The number one mistake
nice guys like you make--

13:51.308 --> 13:52.767
Being too nice.

13:53.227 --> 13:54.811
You can be too nice?

13:54.895 --> 13:57.188
Yep. If you want to
keep her interested,

13:57.272 --> 13:58.731
you have to act aloof,

13:59.108 --> 14:00.900
Like you don't really care
one way or the other.

14:01.235 --> 14:03.361
Well, ok.

14:03.445 --> 14:05.863
Hey, Aang. I was wondering--

14:05.948 --> 14:07.240
See you later.

14:08.992 --> 14:11.577
Wow. That kid is good.

14:12.371 --> 14:14.747
And you'll be fine
as long as you've got a scarf.

14:15.040 --> 14:16.207
Bye-bye, now.

14:16.542 --> 14:18.918
Ok, ok. But one more thing.

14:19.211 --> 14:21.254
All right. What is it?

14:21.547 --> 14:24.841
Should I eat a mango or a papaya

14:24.925 --> 14:26.092
for breakfast tomorrow?

14:26.176 --> 14:27.593
Papaya.

14:28.262 --> 14:30.263
I hate papaya.

14:30.514 --> 14:32.348
Hey, Katara.

14:32.432 --> 14:33.516
I didn't see you there.

14:33.600 --> 14:35.226
Hey, Aang.

14:35.561 --> 14:36.727
That's ok.

14:36.812 --> 14:38.229
I'm busy with my own stuff.

14:46.905 --> 14:48.656
Papaya, please.

14:49.867 --> 14:51.826
So, papaya.

14:51.910 --> 14:54.036
Would you like some?

14:54.246 --> 14:55.371
You know me.

14:55.455 --> 14:57.123
I don't really care what I eat.

14:57.749 --> 14:58.749
Ok, then.

14:58.834 --> 14:59.876
See you later.

15:02.171 --> 15:03.838
Maybe aloof isn't my style.

15:04.173 --> 15:06.674
A panda lily.

15:07.968 --> 15:09.260
Did you see that?

15:10.846 --> 15:13.806
Excuse me. Where can a guy
find one of those things?

15:15.350 --> 15:17.476
I can't believe you're
dragging me all the way up here

15:17.561 --> 15:19.061
For a stupid flower.

15:19.146 --> 15:22.064
Not just any flower-- A panda lily.

15:22.274 --> 15:24.650
I've seen it in action,
and, boy, does it work.

15:25.527 --> 15:27.612
Flowers are fine once you're married,

15:27.696 --> 15:29.238
but at this early stage,

15:29.323 --> 15:32.366
it's critical that you maintain
maximum aloofness.

15:33.493 --> 15:35.119
But my heart
is telling me to get this flower,

15:35.370 --> 15:37.371
And Aunt Wu said
if I trusted my heart,

15:37.456 --> 15:38.998
I would be with the one I love.

15:39.499 --> 15:42.752
What? Don't tell me
you believe in that stuff, too.

15:43.378 --> 15:46.047
Well, Aunt Wu hasn't been wrong yet.

15:46.131 --> 15:47.673
Why should she be wrong about love?

15:50.302 --> 15:51.552
There, on the rim!

15:57.059 --> 15:58.684
Oh, no.

15:59.228 --> 16:00.436
Aunt Wu was wrong.

16:12.532 --> 16:13.741
Those people all think they're safe.

16:13.825 --> 16:15.284
We've got to warn them.

16:15.619 --> 16:16.827
There's no time to walk.

16:17.079 --> 16:18.079
Grab on.

16:18.163 --> 16:19.288
Aah!

16:28.548 --> 16:29.840
Hi, Katara.

16:29.925 --> 16:31.926
Can you believe she won't let me in?

16:32.177 --> 16:33.636
And after all the business
I've given her?

16:33.929 --> 16:35.096
But she doesn't even charge.

16:35.597 --> 16:36.722
I know, but still.

16:37.182 --> 16:39.225
Well, we have other things
to worry about.

16:39.309 --> 16:41.269
Aunt Wu was wrong about the volcano.

16:41.603 --> 16:44.188
Sokka, you tried to convince me
she was wrong before.

16:44.273 --> 16:45.731
It's gonna take an awful lot
to change my--

16:47.943 --> 16:49.068
Oh, no.

16:50.362 --> 16:53.155
Everyone, that volcano
is gonna blow any second!

16:53.615 --> 16:55.449
Aunt Wu was wrong!

16:55.534 --> 16:58.494
Yeah, yeah. We know
you don't believe in Aunt Wu,

16:58.578 --> 17:00.204
Mr. Science and Reason lover.

17:00.622 --> 17:03.499
If you won't listen to him,
maybe you'll listen to me.

17:03.834 --> 17:06.460
I want to believe Aunt Wu and her
predictions as much as you do,

17:06.545 --> 17:08.754
but my brother and Aang saw the lava

17:08.839 --> 17:10.089
with their own eyes.

17:10.173 --> 17:14.844
Well, I heard Aunt Wu's prediction
with my own ears.

17:15.971 --> 17:17.305
Please listen to us!

17:17.389 --> 17:19.015
You are all in danger,

17:19.099 --> 17:21.058
and we have to get out of here!

17:21.143 --> 17:23.185
You can't rely
on Aunt Wu's predictions!

17:23.520 --> 17:26.105
You have to take fate
into your own hands!

17:26.940 --> 17:27.940
Look!

17:28.025 --> 17:29.942
Can your fortune-telling explain that?

17:32.529 --> 17:35.573
Heh. Can your science
explain why it rains?

17:35.907 --> 17:38.242
Yes! Yes, it can!

17:42.831 --> 17:44.749
They just won't listen to reason.

17:44.958 --> 17:47.251
But they will listen to Aunt Wu.

17:47.461 --> 17:49.128
I know. That's the problem.

17:49.338 --> 17:51.714
Well, it's about to become
the solution.

17:51.798 --> 17:53.841
We're taking fate in our own hands.

17:54.134 --> 17:56.635
First, I need to borrow
Aunt Wu's cloud-reading book.

18:06.396 --> 18:07.772
Shh.

18:07.856 --> 18:10.191
We don't want anyone to hear us.

18:10.567 --> 18:13.778
Oh! Oh, I didn't see you there.

18:14.279 --> 18:15.780
You don't like me, do you?

18:16.114 --> 18:17.531
Of course I like you.

18:17.908 --> 18:19.658
But not the way I like you.

18:20.619 --> 18:22.870
Oh. I guess not.

18:23.330 --> 18:24.830
It's ok.

18:24.915 --> 18:27.583
It's just really hard
when you like someone,

18:27.667 --> 18:30.211
but they don't think of you that way.

18:30.420 --> 18:32.046
I know what you mean.

18:32.255 --> 18:33.714
She's beautiful, by the way.

18:34.925 --> 18:36.634
That water tribe girl.

18:36.718 --> 18:38.636
I can see why you like her so much.

18:39.262 --> 18:41.305
She's sweet, she's a bender,

18:41.390 --> 18:45.309
and her hair seems so manageable.

18:46.478 --> 18:47.686
Don't worry.

18:47.771 --> 18:49.105
You're gonna meet a great guy

18:49.189 --> 18:50.523
who's gonna completely fall for you.

18:50.607 --> 18:51.607
I know it.

18:51.691 --> 18:52.858
Thanks.

18:53.610 --> 18:54.610
Wait.

18:54.820 --> 18:55.945
Don't you want this?

18:56.947 --> 18:58.197
How did you know?

18:58.281 --> 19:00.783
I've kind of been stalking you. Heh.

19:01.618 --> 19:02.910
Thanks...

19:03.120 --> 19:04.745
I guess.

19:07.541 --> 19:09.166
Clouds are made
of water and air,

19:09.709 --> 19:10.960
So between the two of us,

19:11.044 --> 19:13.546
we ought to be able to bend them
into any shape we want.

19:14.089 --> 19:17.007
I found it--
The symbol for volcanic doom.

19:44.119 --> 19:45.953
Aunt Wu, look!

19:46.663 --> 19:48.330
Something's happening in the clouds!

19:48.623 --> 19:49.915
That's very strange.

19:50.000 --> 19:52.751
It shouldn't-- Oh, my!

20:01.011 --> 20:03.429
We could still save the village
if we act fast.

20:03.847 --> 20:05.181
Sokka has a plan.

20:05.265 --> 20:07.641
Lava is gonna flow
downhill to this spot.

20:07.726 --> 20:09.185
If we can dig a deep enough trench,

20:09.269 --> 20:11.187
we can channel all the lava
away from the village

20:11.271 --> 20:12.271
to the river.

20:12.355 --> 20:14.690
If any of you are earth benders,
come with me.

20:15.108 --> 20:16.108
I'm an earth bender!

20:16.193 --> 20:17.193
I'm not!

20:17.569 --> 20:19.028
Everybody else, grab a shovel.

20:20.489 --> 20:21.655
Come on! We've got to hurry.

20:41.218 --> 20:42.968
Dig faster! Dig faster!

20:47.682 --> 20:49.642
Everyone needs to evacuate!

20:49.726 --> 20:50.893
We'll come for you when it's safe!

21:20.215 --> 21:21.382
It's too much.

21:21.466 --> 21:22.550
It's gonna overflow!

21:22.634 --> 21:23.634
Aah!

21:37.732 --> 21:38.941
Aah!

21:56.668 --> 21:57.668
Man...

21:58.044 --> 22:00.921
Sometimes I forget
what a powerful bender that kid is.

22:01.006 --> 22:02.965
Wait, what did you just say?

22:03.049 --> 22:05.301
Nothing. Just that Aang
is one powerful bender.

22:09.973 --> 22:12.099
I suppose he is.

22:17.731 --> 22:20.316
By the way,
we kind of borrowed your book.

22:20.650 --> 22:23.110
So you messed with the clouds,
did you?

22:24.070 --> 22:27.197
Ha ha ha! Very clever.

22:27.616 --> 22:29.908
No offense, but I hope this
has taught everyone a lesson

22:29.993 --> 22:32.536
about not relying too much
on fortune-telling.

22:32.746 --> 22:35.414
But Aunt Wu predicted
the village wouldn't be destroyed,

22:35.498 --> 22:36.582
and it wasn't.

22:37.000 --> 22:38.542
She was right, after all.

22:38.627 --> 22:40.336
I hate you.

22:40.420 --> 22:41.920
It's ok, Sokka.

22:42.005 --> 22:43.881
Everything's gonna be all right.

22:44.090 --> 22:45.341
Can I ask you something?

22:45.425 --> 22:47.217
Of course, honey.

22:47.302 --> 22:49.678
You didn't really see love
in my fortune, did you?

22:49.763 --> 22:51.722
You just told me
what I wanted to hear.

22:52.015 --> 22:54.391
I'll tell you a little secret,
young airbender.

22:54.809 --> 22:57.394
Just as you reshaped those clouds,

22:57.646 --> 23:00.981
you have the power
to shape your own destiny.

23:02.150 --> 23:03.317
Good-bye, everyone!

23:03.401 --> 23:05.152
It was so nice to meet you!

23:05.654 --> 23:06.987
Take care, Meng.

23:07.072 --> 23:08.238
Take care!

23:12.786 --> 23:13.911
Floozy.
